{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Stones</b> — The waters wear away stones over long periods of time." "<b>Its torrents</b> — It refers to the channel of the waters, and the sense is: its torrents wash away its earth; so is the hope of man destroyed in his death."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "Resolved ספיחיה as referring to water torrents/channels based on the following gloss שבולת המים; the literal sense of the lemma and the phrase 'its earth' (עפר) preserved hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:38.529789997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}